--TEST--
`Core\Command::run` throws for a `#[Command]` parameter no argument's text is converted into yet, rather than guessing — ADR 0086 § 6
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 6 admits `decimal` among the types an argument may be given at, and this
// runtime does not convert one yet. The two wrong answers are a plausible zero
// and a usage error blaming the command line, so it is neither: a `LogicError`,
// which is what a mistake in the *program* is, since the table is fixed at
// compile time and no input can change what this row declares.
class Ledger {
    #[Core\Command(name: "deposit")]
    public static function deposit(decimal $amount): uint {
        echo "deposit ran\n";
        return 0;
    }
}

try {
    uint $status = Core\Command::run();
    echo "status: ", $status, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--ARGS--
deposit
1.50
--EXPECT--
`Core\Command::run` cannot convert an argument into the type `deposit`'s `amount` is declared at yet
